`deploy_stack()` only passes `-c ip_blocks=...` when `ip_blocks` is non-empty, which makes it impossible to explicitly override/clear an `IP_BLOCKS` environment variable (or a default context value) back to empty. This can lead to unexpected extra CIDRs being included in the allowlist. Consider always passing `ip_blocks` context (even if empty) or adding an explicit sentinel/flag to mean “no supplemental blocks”.
