```

For `stack_type == "frontend"`, `deploy_stack()` passes `-c ip_blocks=...`, but the frontend CDK app/stack reads supplemental CIDRs from `additional_ips` / `ADDITIONAL_IPS` (not `ip_blocks`). As-is, `--ip-blocks` will have no effect on the frontend allowlist behavior. Either rename frontend’s parameter to `ip_blocks` for consistency, or update `deploy.py` to pass `additional_ips` when deploying the frontend stack.
```suggestion
    if stack_type == "webbffsse":
        cmd.extend(["-c", f"limit_ips={str(limit_ips).lower()}"])
        if ip_blocks:
            cmd.extend(["-c", f"ip_blocks={ip_blocks}"])

    if stack_type == "frontend":
        cmd.extend(["-c", f"limit_ips={str(limit_ips).lower()}"])
        if ip_blocks:
            cmd.extend(["-c", f"additional_ips={ip_blocks}"])
```
